# GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3 on 2x NVIDIA DGX Spark (GB10) — single source of configuration.
# Copy to .env and edit. .env is gitignored (it may carry an HF token).
#
#   cp env.example .env
#
# Every non-default value below is a deliberate, measured choice — docs/02-parameters.md
# explains each one. Values marked PROD are what this cluster actually runs.

# --- nodes --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything ssh can resolve from the head node. The head runs rank 0 and start.sh
# drives the worker over ssh (one oneshot systemd unit owns BOTH ranks).
WORKER_SSH=nvidia@spark2            # ssh target for the worker node
WORKER_USER=nvidia
WORKER_HOME=/home/nvidia

# --- the 200Gb QSFP link ------------------------------------------------------
# PROD: rail 1 on BOTH nodes. Do NOT copy upstream's asymmetric interface pins
# (enp1s0f0np0 / rocep1s0f0 are DOWN on this hardware — NCCL init hangs).
# start.sh preflights that NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX names a populated GID on both nodes
# (an all-zero entry kills the worker rank ~60s in with ibv_modify_qp errno 61).
HEAD_CX7_IF=enp1s0f1np1
WORKER_CX7_IF=enp1s0f1np1
# IB device names must be pinned TOO — start.sh's vendored default keeps
# upstream's asymmetric WORKER_CX7_IB=rocep1s0f0 (DOWN on this hardware), and
# the GID preflight then refuses the boot. Found by the v1.0.1 reproduce test.
HEAD_CX7_IB=rocep1s0f1
WORKER_CX7_IB=rocep1s0f1
HEAD_IP=192.168.177.10
WORKER_IP=192.168.177.11
NCCL_IB_HCA=rocep1s0f1

# --- model + image ------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL=brandonmusic/GLM-5.3-Flash-tr3-4bpw      # GLM-5.3-Flash 320B MoE, EXL3/TR3 4bpw, 120 shards
MODEL_REVISION=1ae6d70430a12d762917786696db06a7b4f9bbae
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3
# Pin the API port: the vendored start.sh default is upstream's 8888, but every
# probe/test in this kit (acceptance, serving-test, benches) defaults to 8000.
# Found by the v1.0.1 reproduce test — without this, a fresh boot lands on 8888.
PORT=8000
# PROD since 2026-08-30 is a local Dockerfile build, not a pulled artifact.
# After `docker build -t glm53-selfbuild .` (README), this name matches.
# Production currently runs the tagged build `glm53-selfbuild:b5ab8091-s2b`.
# Last public GHCR digest (pre-kernel-stack, no exl3_fat_gemm — leave the
# EXL3_FAT_* flags off if you boot it):
# IMAGE=ghcr.io/miaai-lab/glm-5.3-flash-2x-dgx-sparks@sha256:9bb1557a4234fce63d59599e44d10747eabd742beb337eebf9e7070be8a0fd58
IMAGE=glm53-selfbuild
SKIP_PULL=1
# HF_TOKEN=                          # only needed for gated repos; keep out of git

# --- serving shape (PROD values, 2026-08-29 1M window) ------------------------
# 1M allocates since the drafter/MLA page slot-share landed: the SAME pinned KV
# pool now counts 1,396,551 tokens = 1.40x a full 1M request (1.22x @262k before —
# pool "tokens" are geometry-dependent, the bytes never move). Costs ~6-9% prose
# decode + longer cold prefill; structured decode unaffected. Solo-session cache
# retention verified to ~340k tokens at 99%; multi-session retention works since
# the sparse-retention adoption below (2x68k at 97.8%) — compact sessions around
# 300k, the measured solo ceiling (docs/04-prefix-caching.md).
MAX_MODEL_LEN=1000000
# 3584 = the attention/mamba page size of this hybrid (KDA) model. Align-mode
# prefix caching NEEDS chunk ends on page boundaries: MNBT < 3584 silently
# yields ~0% cache hits. 8192 OOMs the GB10 indexer smem on long prefill.
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=3584
MAX_NUM_SEQS=4
# Long-prefill chunk cap (PROD since 2026-08-29): a long prefill takes only this
# many tokens per step, so short requests co-schedule instead of queueing behind
# it — measured TTFT for a 1.2k request behind a 240k cold prefill: 256s -> 7.9s,
# for -5.1% solo cold-prefill throughput (any value < 3584 costs 2 steps/page;
# 1792 = clean half-page alternation). Unset to disable. Decode and prefix-cache
# retention are unaffected.
LONG_PREFILL_TOKEN_THRESHOLD=1792
# Server-side default for requests that omit max_tokens (W16). Empty = stock
# unbounded fallback (max_model_len - prompt). Own --override-generation-config
# arg, hash-neutral; the model's generation_config temperature 1.0 is kept.
# DEFAULT_MAX_NEW_TOKENS=65536
# W17 opt-in: shrink vLLM SpinCondition reader spin 1 s -> 2 ms (GB10 core relief).
# GLM53_SPINWAIT_2MS=1
# W18 (issue #16): exempt KpoolTailManager from the partial-hash veto -> prefix hits at
# hash grain 64 instead of the 3584-token page. Without it, prompts under one page
# can NEVER hit and vllm:prefix_cache_hits_total stays 0 on a sub-page workload —
# that is the floor, not a broken cache. Production runs 1 (cost ~3% structured
# decode). 0 reverts without a JIT wipe. The on-ready banner prints apc_grain=.
GLM53_FINE_GRAINED_APC=1
# Align-floor overlay (overlay/patch_align_floor.py): when LPTT >= the 3584 page, the
# mamba align split floors a sub-block mixed-prefill chunk to 0 tokens -> the held
# request makes no progress while a peer decodes (bounded by the peer's decode, not
# infinite). 1 = floor at the mixed cap instead. Dormant at LPTT=1792 (the helper is
# never reached); required before any LPTT >= 3584 arm. Read once at import: flipping
# it needs a restart. Not in the JIT shape hash. Rollback GLM53_ALIGN_FLOOR=0.
GLM53_ALIGN_FLOOR=1
# W41 KV-capacity boot log (overlay/patch_kv_capacity_log.py, kit PR #94): log-only.
# After the stock "GPU KV cache size" line, prints one line per KV-cache group
# (spec, block_size, page bytes, ids per 1M request, prefix-cacheable, eagle/mamba
# mode) plus the usable-block-id count and an aligned dense-retention
# cached-conversation upper bound. Diagnostic only: exceptions are caught and logged,
# never raised. Exactly 0 or 1; validated on start/restart, so a bad value
# never blocks stop/status/logs on a running pair. Not in the JIT hash.
GLM53_KV_CAPACITY_LOG=1
# W42 per-request prefix-cache no-store (overlay/patch_apc_no_store.py, kit PR #95).
# A request sent with vllm_xargs {"skip_writing_prefix_cache": 1} (or the typed
# SamplingParams field) never inserts its blocks into the GPU prefix cache; lookups
# are unaffected. Its blocks stay unhashed and recycle LIFO from the front of the free
# queue, so a one-off batch lane no longer evicts other sessions' cached prefixes.
# 0 = kill switch: a valid 1 becomes a logged no-op (malformed values are still
# rejected with HTTP 400 at the API boundary). Exactly 0 or 1. Not in the JIT hash.
GLM53_APC_NO_STORE=1
# W28 sparse-indexer workspace experiment. The overlay is GLM-5.3-only:
# it is activated from models/glm5next/nvidia/attention.py with that model
# instance's index_kpool, so the DFlash2 drafter and other model paths retain
# the generic stock allocation. `stock` is production before the window;
# `rightsize` uses MAX_NUM_SEQS * cdiv((MAX_MODEL_LEN + draft k), index_kpool).
# At the current 1M / seqs=4 / kpool=4 / k=7 geometry this predicts 1,000,008
# entries (~126.9 MiB including radix scratch) instead of 40,000,000
# (5036.40 MiB). The arm must produce matching lines on both ranks and no
# row/chunk guard failure. Reclaim first; never raise the KV pin in this window.
GLM53_INDEXER_WORKSPACE=stock
# W23 mixed-prefill gate v2 (defaults shown; MAX_WAIT_MS=0 restores the v1 hold-forever gate).
# Cached follow-ups whose uncached remainder is <= WARM_TOKENS skip the mixing hold entirely;
# a cold prefill held while others decode proceeds after MAX_WAIT_MS at LATE_CAP tokens/step.
# GLM53_MIXED_PREFILL_WARM_TOKENS=3584
# GLM53_MIXED_PREFILL_MAX_WAIT_MS=1500
# GLM53_MIXED_PREFILL_LATE_CAP=512
# W26 gate v3 — aging for a late-admitted cold read (0 = flat v2 crawl). Once past
# MAX_WAIT_MS the cap doubles every ESCALATE_MS up to LATE_CAP_MAX (1792 = the
# long-prefill chunk ceiling, LONG_PREFILL_TOKEN_THRESHOLD): on this MoE the per-step
# cost is mostly expert-weight streaming, so a flat 512 cap multiplies expensive steps
# and taxes running decodes for longer. The late path logs late-admit / late-escalate /
# late-done lines (grep "decode-floor-v3"). Not in the JIT shape hash.
# Measured (W26, 2x DGX Spark, 60k cold read against a running decoder): aging on vs
# off = read 78.3 -> 63.1 s, decode tokens per 240 s 677 -> 863 (+27%), short TTFT
# behind a 240k read 6.93 -> 6.65 s, gap p99 1.39 -> 1.78 s. A flat LATE_CAP=1024
# reaches the same throughput but costs every short late read (gap p50 1.07 vs 0.71 s,
# TTFT 7.58 s) -- prefer aging. Set ESCALATE_MS=0 to roll back to v2.
GLM53_MIXED_PREFILL_ESCALATE_MS=10000
#GLM53_MIXED_PREFILL_LATE_CAP_MAX=1792
# W27 (kit PR #87): server-side default reasoning effort for clients that omit
# chat_template_kwargs.reasoning_effort. The template maps UNSET -> Max (the most
# expensive setting), so a client that sends only enable_thinking runs at Max.
# low | high | max; empty = send no flag (template renders Max). Per-request kwargs
# override. Changes token ~2 of every prompt for clients that omit it -> one-time
# prefix-cache fork; clients that pin a different value keep a separate prefix.
# Not in the JIT shape hash. Measured 2026-09-01: decode benches unchanged
# (structured 69.1-69.4 @ 1.0000/7.0, prose 29.2-31.0); thinking-on probe, High vs
# Max: 297/1636, 542/1181, 492/2002 completion tokens, wall 9/68, 14/29, 26/83 s.
# Quality at High for long agentic tasks is NOT yet established on this stack -- the
# owner's coding client pins max explicitly until the blind paired test passes.
GLM53_DEFAULT_REASONING_EFFORT=high
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8                  # packed fp8_ds_mla
GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.85                   # BOOT GATE ONLY under the KV pin; 0.87 crash-loops
# KV pool pinned: profiling skipped, pool byte-identical every boot. Suggested by
# vLLM's own first unpinned boot. NEVER raise it (no fit protection under the pin;
# measured MemFree under burst load: 3.6 GiB; a full 900k request bottomed the
# head node at 2.95 GiB). Keep the QUOTED form.
# --no-async-scheduling is REQUIRED: async double-counts the SW-family reservation
# (vLLM #47728 class) and the admission check at this geometry fails the 14.36 GiB pin.
EXTRA_ARGS="--kv-cache-memory-bytes 15414698763 --no-async-scheduling"

# --- prefix caching -----------------------------------------------------------
# Sparse KDA (mamba) state retention: 0 = keep only replay boundaries and
# shared-prefix junctions (Marconi-style). PROD since 2026-08-29 — this single
# knob fixed BOTH hybrid prefix-cache failure modes on this stack: two 68k
# sessions went 0% -> 97.8% cross-session hits, and concurrent (co-batched)
# prefill insertion went 0% -> 95%. Solo replay held 98%. Unset = dense
# retention = cached pages too expensive, multi-session thrash returns.
# Must be 0 or a multiple of the 3584 page size. docs/04-prefix-caching.md.
# W25 (2026-09-01): production now runs the GLOBAL knob DENSE (line commented out)
# with the drafter alone sparse via _SWA=0 below — +37–49% hits on shared-prefix/
# different-length prompts (subagent forks); costs ~25 pp only at 4×200k concurrent
# replays. Uncomment to return to boundaries-only for every group.
#VLLM_PREFIX_CACHE_RETENTION_INTERVAL=0

# W25 — per-group drafter retention (overlay/patch_apc_per_group_retention.py).
# The DFlash2 drafter SWA group hashes 33 of the 38 block ids a cached 3584-token
# segment costs, for a group whose hit length the hybrid min() discards anyway.
# "0" keeps only reachable boundaries for THAT group; other groups keep the
# global value above. Unset = overlay's automatic rule. Not in the JIT shape hash.
VLLM_PREFIX_CACHE_RETENTION_INTERVAL_SWA=0

# --- speculative decoding -----------------------------------------------------
SPEC_METHOD=dflash
DFLASH_MODEL=incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2
# Pinned drafter checkpoint. incoai has shipped three different model.safetensors
# under Hub main (08-27 7d74cdd, 08-28 dc77ff1, 08-31 bf582e4); every receipt in
# this repo was taken on 7d74cdd. A drafter swap is a JIT-shape change (hashed by
# local/prod-start.sh). Empty = track main deliberately.
DFLASH_REVISION=7d74cdd881ed7e32c31175984a67823127b66cfe
DFLASH_TOKENS=7                     # k=7; verify batch = 8 tokens/seq — cudagraph capture
                                    # sizes 1 2 4 8 16 24 32 are TOKEN batches for 1-4 seqs

# --- downloads / sync ---------------------------------------------------------
# HF CLI override when `hf` lives outside PATH (venv installs). May contain
# arguments. Without it start.sh falls back to `python3 -m
# huggingface_hub.commands.huggingface_cli` when huggingface_hub is importable.
# HF_BIN=/home/you/.hf-cli/venv/bin/hf
# Force the ~164 GiB rsync even when the worker revision marker matches:
# FORCE_SYNC=1

# --- API auth -------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI-compatible bearer token. vLLM reads VLLM_API_KEY natively (fallback when
# --api-key is absent on the CLI), so the key never lands in argv / the startup
# log. Empty = unauthenticated. This kit binds to 127.0.0.1 only either way —
# the token is defense-in-depth, not the primary boundary.
# VLLM_API_KEY=

# --- timeouts -----------------------------------------------------------------
READY_TIMEOUT=4800                  # cold JIT after a cache wipe is slow, not dead
VLLM_EXECUTE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1800

# --- W24 + S2a/S2b: fat-expert prefill + ticket scheduler (PROD = all on) -----
# Higher fat tiers imply the lower ones. All three ON in production since
# 2026-08-31 (W24); the CUDA kernel is baked by this repo's Dockerfile (fat
# GEMM + the 2026-09-02 3-stage cp.async pipeline + the d5e4361 ticket
# scheduler). Require the self-built image: the GHCR digest above does not
# export exl3_fat_gemm, so KERNEL=1 on that pin fails at start. Off = the
# pre-W24 fused-MoE path on a rebuilt image; GHCR users must leave these
# commented.
EXL3_FAT_SORTED=1     # contiguous expert slices of the existing sort
EXL3_FAT_BATCHED=1    # E1: persistent scratch + concatenated gate+up trellis
EXL3_FAT_KERNEL=1     # E2: fused direct/scatter trellis GEMM (SM121; pipelined)
